@tradition every-song
// Every song (FX14, 0.92.5 item 16; SW1's pitch): Saturdays before dinner, the five who know every song in the record
// cabinet sing through it in the music room, one record at a time, arguing about the second verse. Behind WEEKEND_ON.
k: 459
title: Every song
when: weekly saturday
at: 17:00-17:50
min: 20
jitter: 10
where: 4 pool music
hold: 1
who: torres-zeke always, takahashi-wen always, farouk-olu always, achterberg-lars always, haddad-tamsin always, musician 50%, music 50%, everyone 6%
anim: musician play, everyone talk
host: torres-zeke
from: torres-zeke

== mail
- Every song, tomorrow at {time}, the music room. This week: the lighthouse one. I'm right about the second verse. Come and tell Takahashi.

== ask
- Every song tonight. Five people, one record, five different sets of words.   #funny
- Coming to the music room before dinner? Everyone sings. Nobody agrees.   #funny
- Sing-along at five. You don't need to know the words. Nobody does.   #funny

== here
- It's "light". The light came home. I've said it for a year.   #funny
- Second verse. Here it comes. Brace yourselves.   #funny
- Everyone in for the chorus. Even you at the back.
- Takahashi's singing the other words again. Loudly.   #funny

== thanks
- You squeeze in by the record cabinet. A record goes on, five people start the same song with different words, and by the chorus the whole room sings whichever is loudest.

== chatter
- Every song ran over. The second verse took twenty minutes.   #funny
- Achterberg brought sheet music to Every song. Nobody could read it. We sang anyway.   #funny
- I went to Every song not knowing a single word. Turns out that's normal.   #warm
